80 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/ROW'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Rowing at the 1904 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "29 – 30 July 1904"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "5"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Non-medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "7"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/208"} "Creve Coeur Lake, Maryland Heights"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The 1904 rowing events were held at " [:a {:href "/venues/208"} "Creve Coeur Lake"] ".  They were contested on 29 and 30 July 1904 as part of the Olympic Games.  The bulk of the entrants were from the United States, although the Toronto Argonaut Club did send an eight-oar crew which competed in the " [:a {:href "/results/157532"} "Olympic senior eight-oared shells"] ".  The events doubled as the United States Championships of the National Association of Amateur Oarsmen (NAAO)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In addition to the Olympic events, multiple ancillary events were contested, such as " [:a {:href "/results/926078"} "association single sculls"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/926086"} "intermediate eight-oared shells"] ", " [:a {:href "/results/926073"} "intermediate single sculls"] ", and " [:a {:href "/results/926084"} "intermediate coxless pairs"] ".  The Americans dominated, with the only foreign competitors in the events that are usually considered of Olympic caliber having been the Toronto Argonauts’ coxed eight.  There were other entrants from Canada, as well as from Germany, in the ancillary events.  These cannot be considered Olympic caliber because they were essentially restricted events for rowers of lesser skill."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The " [:a {:href "/results/157528"} "single sculls event"] " had the potential to be a great event for the time as the world’s top two amateur scullers, " [:a {:href "/athletes/892365"} "James Ten Eyck"] " (USA) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36263"} "Lou Scholes"] " (CAN), both entered.  Scholes had won the Diamond Sculls at Henley earlier in the year, but neither he nor the American champion Ten Eyck participated."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Creve Couer Lake still exists today.  In 1995, during the filming of some television shows concerning Olympic history, one of our members (" [:a {:href "/athletes/1200809"} "Bill Mallon"] ") had the opportunity to spend part of an afternoon there.  It is still the training grounds of several of the St. Louis rowing clubs.  When he told one of the local fishermen that the 1904 Olympic rowing events had been contested here, his comment was that of incredulity. “This place?  It’s just a mud hole.”  Perhaps.  But, for two days in 1904, it was a very famous mud hole."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All the races were over 1½ miles (2,414.02 metres).  The schedules say that the fours and eights were held straightaway, while the pairs and both sculls rowed out 3/4 mile (1,207.01 metres), turned, and then rowed back over the same course. However, if one sees the Creve Coeur Lake in person (as Mallon has), the lake is simply not long enough for a 1½ mile straightaway course, so there had to be a turn for all events. It is possible that a straight course was scheduled but it is much more likely that there were turns for all events."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157528"} "Single Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 July 1904"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157529"} "Double Sculls, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 July 1904"] "\n" [:td {} "6"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157530"} "Coxless Pairs, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "29 July 1904"] "\n" [:td {} "6"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157531"} "Coxless Fours, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "29 July 1904"] "\n" [:td {} "12"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/157532"} "Eights, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "30 July 1904"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n" [:td {} "2"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n44 (44/0)\n"] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n2 (2/0)\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Non-medal events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/9017151"} "Coxless Fours, International, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic (non-medal)"] "\n" [:td {} "30 July 1904"] "\n" [:td {} "8"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/926073"} "Single Sc